   "text": "This is the 7\u2011tert\u2011butyldimethylsilyl, 10\u2011hydroxy derivative of camptothecin, the structure known as DB\u201167.\n\n- **Core:** the pentacyclic camptothecin framework is a quinoline fused to a pyrrolo\u2011pyridone, which is fused to the \u03b1\u2011hydroxy lactone ring. The lactone has a C=O and an ring O\u2013CH2.\n- **Quaternary stereocentre:** it carries an ethyl group and a hashed OH, and is bonded to the lactone C=O and to the ring carbon on the pyridone side. From the hash and the positions of the other three substituents, I assign it `@@` in the SMILES order written below.\n- **Quinoline substituents:** an OH sits on the benzo ring, and a Si(CH3)2\u2013C(CH3)3 group sits on the quinoline carbon next to the CH2.\n\nI traced the quinoline ring atom by atom against the drawing to place the OH and the silyl group.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@@]1(O)C(=O)OCc2c1cc1-c3nc4ccc(O)cc4c([Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)c3Cn1c2=O"
